*> Lane bugbeditem (T62600 and on; operator try19: "a bed renders in the hand and in the inventory wrong"): the item definition of a bed is a `minecraft:composite` of two block models
*> (52 sections 5.3 to 5.5: block/<colour>_bed_head as it is, block/<colour>_bed_foot translated one block along z; the straw bed turned 180 degrees about Y), so the generic path drew only its
*> first member, the head half, as a squat cube. The bed is now a code-drawn kind (SPECIAL-ITEM-KIND 5, SPECIAL-BED-QUADS): both halves, in the slot, in the hand and on the ground, under the
*> display table of block/template_bed (52 5.3). The expected quads come from the independent script client/tests/fixtures/gen_bed_item.py (the JSON of the generated vanilla pack, CC_GENERATED_DIR):
*> the model rows are the 30 faces of white_bed in the unit cell (texture, corners x y z and uv times 1000), the GUI rows the 13 quads that face the viewer under display.gui (texture,
*> brightness times 10000, the corners' x, y in the 16 pixel cell, uv).
