 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-GEN
     ACCEPT WS-GEN FROM ENVIRONMENT "CC_GENERATED_DIR"
     IF WS-GEN = SPACES
         MOVE "/tmp/cc-test/generated" TO WS-GEN
     END-IF
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-ROOT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-GEN) "/vanilla-resources" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-ROOT
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "PACK-STACK-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     ADD 1 TO PK-COUNT
     INITIALIZE PK-PACK(PK-COUNT)
     MOVE 1 TO PK-KIND(PK-COUNT)
     MOVE 3 TO PK-LEVEL(PK-COUNT)
     MOVE "generated/vanilla" TO PK-ID(PK-COUNT)
     MOVE 17 TO PK-ID-LENGTH(PK-COUNT)
     MOVE WS-ROOT TO PK-ROOT(PK-COUNT)
     MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ROOT)) TO PK-ROOT-LENGTH(PK-COUNT)
     CALL "PACK-STACK-OPEN" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "PACK-SOURCE-FILES" USING CLIENT-STATE PK-COUNT
     CALL "ATLAS-BUILD" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE 256 TO PL-HEIGHT
     MOVE 0 TO SK-U
     MOVE 1 TO CL-GUI-SCALE
     MOVE CT-TYPE-STANDARD TO CT-SET-TYPE
     CALL "CONTENT-SET-COUNTS"
     MOVE 1 TO CT-OPEN
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     MOVE "white_bed" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-WHITE WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     MOVE "straw_bed" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-STRAW WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     MOVE "red_bed" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-RED WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     MOVE "blue_bed" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-BLUE WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     MOVE "dirt" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-DIRT WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     PERFORM CHECK-KINDS
     PERFORM CHECK-MODEL
     PERFORM CHECK-STRAW
     PERFORM CHECK-GUI
     PERFORM CHECK-COLOURS
     PERFORM CHECK-HAND
     PERFORM CHECK-GROUND
     STOP RUN.

*> The kind of an item: 5 for a bed with the two model ids and the straw flag, 0 for dirt and the chest.
 CHECK-KINDS.
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "bugbeitems white_bed is the code-drawn kind 5" TO TL-CASE
     CALL "SPECIAL-ITEM-KIND" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-WHITE WS-KIND WS-ID WS-ID-LEN WS-ID2 WS-LEN2 WS-DYE
     MOVE 5 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-KIND TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "S" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "bugbeitems white_bed: the head model id" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "minecraft:block/white_bed_head" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-ID(1:WS-ID-LEN) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "bugbeitems white_bed: the foot model id" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "minecraft:block/white_bed_foot" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-ID2(1:WS-LEN2) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "bugbeitems white_bed is not turned" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-DYE TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "SPECIAL-ITEM-KIND" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-STRAW WS-KIND WS-ID WS-ID-LEN WS-ID2 WS-LEN2 WS-DYE
     MOVE "bugbeitems straw_bed is kind 5 and turned" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 15 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = WS-KIND * 3 + WS-DYE - 1
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "S" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "bugbeitems straw_bed: the foot model id" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "minecraft:block/straw_bed_foot" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-ID2(1:WS-LEN2) TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "SPECIAL-ITEM-KIND" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-DIRT WS-KIND WS-ID WS-ID-LEN WS-ID2 WS-LEN2 WS-DYE
     MOVE "bugbeitems dirt is not code-drawn" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-KIND TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

*> The 30 faces of white_bed in the unit cell: every row of the script is one quad of SQ-TABLE (corners within 0.002, the texture coordinates of the row's sprite).
 CHECK-MODEL.
     CALL "SPECIAL-ITEM-QUADS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-WHITE SQ-TABLE
     MOVE "bugbeitems white_bed: 30 quads, both halves (head 15 faces, foot 15 faces)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 30 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE SQ-COUNT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-BAD
     PERFORM VARYING WS-R FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-R > 30
         MOVE 0 TO WS-FOUND
         PERFORM VARYING WS-Q FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-Q > SQ-COUNT
             PERFORM MODEL-DIFF
             IF WS-MISS = 0
                 ADD 1 TO WS-FOUND
             END-IF
         END-PERFORM
         IF WS-FOUND = 0
             ADD 1 TO WS-BAD
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "bugbeitems white_bed: every expected face (corners, uv) is a quad of the model" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-BAD TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-BAD
     PERFORM VARYING WS-Q FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-Q > SQ-COUNT
         COMPUTE WS-GOT = SQ-T(WS-Q, 1) + SQ-T(WS-Q, 2) + SQ-T(WS-Q, 3)
         IF WS-GOT NOT = 3 OR FUNCTION ABS(SQ-N(WS-Q, 1)) + FUNCTION ABS(SQ-N(WS-Q, 2)) + FUNCTION ABS(SQ-N(WS-Q, 3)) < 0.99
             ADD 1 TO WS-BAD
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "bugbeitems white_bed: white tint and a unit outward normal on every quad" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-BAD TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

*> WS-MISS: how many of the corners and texture coordinates of quad WS-Q differ from model row WS-R.
 MODEL-DIFF.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-MISS
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXID
     MOVE WS-MR-TEX(WS-R) TO WS-TEXID
     MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-TEXID)) TO WS-TEXLEN
     CALL "ATLAS-FIND" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-TEXID WS-TEXLEN WS-TEXSPR
     PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-K > 12
         COMPUTE WS-GOT ROUNDED = SQ-C(WS-Q, WS-K) * 1000
         MOVE WS-MR-V(WS-R, WS-K) TO WS-EXP
         IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-GOT - WS-EXP) > 2
             ADD 1 TO WS-MISS
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-K > 4
         COMPUTE WS-U16 = WS-MR-V(WS-R, 12 + WS-K) / 1000
         COMPUTE WS-V16 = WS-MR-V(WS-R, 16 + WS-K) / 1000
         CALL "ATLAS-UV" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-TEXSPR WS-U16 WS-V16 WS-GU(WS-K) WS-GV(WS-K)
         IF FUNCTION ABS(SQ-U(WS-Q, WS-K) - WS-GU(WS-K)) > 0.0001 OR FUNCTION ABS(SQ-V(WS-Q, WS-K) - WS-GV(WS-K)) > 0.0001
             ADD 1 TO WS-MISS
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     .

*> The straw bed: the 43 faces of its two models, inside the two cells (the 3 pixel frills reach x -3/16 to 19/16), both turned half a turn.
 CHECK-STRAW.
     CALL "SPECIAL-ITEM-QUADS" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-STRAW SQ-TABLE
     MOVE "bugbeitems straw_bed: 43 quads (32 head faces, 11 foot faces)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 43 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE SQ-COUNT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 100 TO WS-XMIN WS-YMIN
     MOVE -100 TO WS-XMAX WS-YMAX
     PERFORM VARYING WS-Q FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-Q > SQ-COUNT
         PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-K > 4
             COMPUTE WS-I = (WS-K - 1) * 3 + 1
             IF SQ-C(WS-Q, WS-I) < WS-XMIN
                 MOVE SQ-C(WS-Q, WS-I) TO WS-XMIN
             END-IF
             IF SQ-C(WS-Q, WS-I) > WS-XMAX
                 MOVE SQ-C(WS-Q, WS-I) TO WS-XMAX
             END-IF
             COMPUTE WS-I = (WS-K - 1) * 3 + 3
             IF SQ-C(WS-Q, WS-I) < WS-YMIN
                 MOVE SQ-C(WS-Q, WS-I) TO WS-YMIN
             END-IF
             IF SQ-C(WS-Q, WS-I) > WS-YMAX
                 MOVE SQ-C(WS-Q, WS-I) TO WS-YMAX
             END-IF
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "bugbeitems straw_bed: x from -0.1875 to 1.1875 (the frills)" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = -1875 + 11875
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N ROUNDED = WS-XMIN * 10000 + WS-XMAX * 10000
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   A zero-thickness face is moved 0.002 of a block out along its normal by ELEMENT-BAKE (the decal rule): the low end may lie that far below 0.
     IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-YMIN) < 0.002
         MOVE 0 TO WS-YMIN
     END-IF
     MOVE "bugbeitems straw_bed: z from 0 to 2.1875, the two halves one behind the other" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = 0 + 21875
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N ROUNDED = WS-YMIN * 10000 + WS-YMAX * 10000
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

*> The slot (18 x 18 at 10, 10, GUI scale 1): the icon cell is at (11, 11). The 13 quads of the script, each found among the slot's quads (sprite, brightness, corners, uv).
 CHECK-GUI.
     MOVE 1 TO SM-WIDGET-COUNT
     MOVE WK-SLOT TO SM-W-KIND(1)
     MOVE 0 TO SM-W-ARG(1) SM-W-STATE(1)
     MOVE 10 TO SM-W-X(1) SM-W-Y(1)
     MOVE 18 TO SM-W-W(1) SM-W-H(1)
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(1)
     MOVE WS-WHITE TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     MOVE 0 TO RL-IC-COUNT
     CALL "UI-RENDER" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE "bugbeitems white_bed in a slot: 13 quads facing the viewer, not the head half as one cube (3 quads)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 13 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = RL-IC-COUNT / 6
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-BAD
     PERFORM VARYING WS-R FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-R > 13
         MOVE 0 TO WS-FOUND
         PERFORM VARYING WS-Q FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-Q > RL-IC-COUNT / 6
             PERFORM GUI-DIFF
             IF WS-MISS = 0
                 ADD 1 TO WS-FOUND
             END-IF
         END-PERFORM
         IF WS-FOUND = 0
             ADD 1 TO WS-BAD
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "bugbeitems white_bed in a slot: every expected quad (sprite, shade, corners in the cell, uv) is drawn" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-BAD TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     PERFORM LOAD-ICONS
     MOVE "bugbeitems white_bed in a slot: every vertex inside the 16 pixel icon cell" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-BAD
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > WS-VN
         IF WS-VX(WS-I) < 11 OR WS-VX(WS-I) > 27 OR WS-VY(WS-I) < 11 OR WS-VY(WS-I) > 27
             ADD 1 TO WS-BAD
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-BAD TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE WS-DIRT TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     MOVE 0 TO RL-IC-COUNT
     CALL "UI-RENDER" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE "bugbeitems dirt in a slot is still its cube (3 quads)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 3 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = RL-IC-COUNT / 6
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE WS-STRAW TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
     MOVE 0 TO RL-IC-COUNT
     CALL "UI-RENDER" USING CLIENT-STATE
     PERFORM LOAD-ICONS
*>   The reference (gen_bed_item.py gui straw_bed): 22 quads facing the viewer, x from 0.125 to 16.461 and y from 3.483 to 16.115 of the cell (the frills reach a little past it).
     MOVE "bugbeitems straw_bed in a slot: 22 quads facing the viewer" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 22 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = RL-IC-COUNT / 6
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 100 TO WS-XMIN WS-YMIN
     MOVE -100 TO WS-XMAX WS-YMAX
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > WS-VN
         MOVE FUNCTION MIN(WS-XMIN, WS-VX(WS-I)) TO WS-XMIN
         MOVE FUNCTION MAX(WS-XMAX, WS-VX(WS-I)) TO WS-XMAX
         MOVE FUNCTION MIN(WS-YMIN, WS-VY(WS-I)) TO WS-YMIN
         MOVE FUNCTION MAX(WS-YMAX, WS-VY(WS-I)) TO WS-YMAX
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "bugbeitems straw_bed in a slot: the icon's extent in the cell (x, y minimum and maximum)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-XMIN - 11.125) > 0.1 OR FUNCTION ABS(WS-XMAX - 27.461) > 0.1
             OR FUNCTION ABS(WS-YMIN - 14.483) > 0.1 OR FUNCTION ABS(WS-YMAX - 27.115) > 0.1
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

*> WS-MISS: how many of the corners, brightness and uv of the slot quad WS-Q (vertices 1, 2, 3 and 6 are its corners) differ from GUI row WS-R.
 GUI-DIFF.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-MISS
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXID
     MOVE WS-GR-TEX(WS-R) TO WS-TEXID
     MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-TEXID)) TO WS-TEXLEN
     CALL "ATLAS-FIND" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-TEXID WS-TEXLEN WS-TEXSPR
     COMPUTE WS-BASE = (WS-Q - 1) * 6
     COMPUTE WS-GOT ROUNDED = RL-IC-B(WS-BASE + 1) * 10000
     MOVE WS-GR-B(WS-R) TO WS-EXP
     IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-GOT - WS-EXP) > 2
         ADD 1 TO WS-MISS
     END-IF
     PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-K > 4
         EVALUATE WS-K
             WHEN 4
                 COMPUTE WS-I = WS-BASE + 6
             WHEN OTHER
                 COMPUTE WS-I = WS-BASE + WS-K
         END-EVALUATE
         COMPUTE WS-GOT ROUNDED = (RL-IC-X(WS-I) - 11) * 1000
         MOVE WS-GR-V(WS-R, WS-K) TO WS-EXP
         IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-GOT - WS-EXP) > 2
             ADD 1 TO WS-MISS
         END-IF
         COMPUTE WS-GOT ROUNDED = (RL-IC-Y(WS-I) - 11) * 1000
         MOVE WS-GR-V(WS-R, WS-K + 4) TO WS-EXP
         IF FUNCTION ABS(WS-GOT - WS-EXP) > 2
             ADD 1 TO WS-MISS
         END-IF
         COMPUTE WS-U16 = WS-GR-V(WS-R, WS-K + 8) / 1000
         COMPUTE WS-V16 = WS-GR-V(WS-R, WS-K + 12) / 1000
         CALL "ATLAS-UV" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-TEXSPR WS-U16 WS-V16 WS-GU(1) WS-GV(1)
         IF FUNCTION ABS(RL-IC-U(WS-I) - WS-GU(1)) > 0.0001 OR FUNCTION ABS(RL-IC-V(WS-I) - WS-GV(1)) > 0.0001
             ADD 1 TO WS-MISS
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     .

 LOAD-ICONS.
     MOVE RL-IC-COUNT TO WS-VN
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > WS-VN
         MOVE RL-IC-U(WS-I) TO WS-VU(WS-I)
         MOVE RL-IC-V(WS-I) TO WS-VV(WS-I)
         MOVE RL-IC-X(WS-I) TO WS-VX(WS-I)
         MOVE RL-IC-Y(WS-I) TO WS-VY(WS-I)
     END-PERFORM
     .

*> WS-IN: how many of the loaded vertices lie in the atlas rectangle of the sprite WS-TEXID names.
 COUNT-IN.
     MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-TEXID)) TO WS-TEXLEN
     CALL "ATLAS-FIND" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-TEXID WS-TEXLEN WS-TEXSPR
     COMPUTE WS-U0 = AT-X(WS-TEXSPR) / AT-W
     COMPUTE WS-U1 = (AT-X(WS-TEXSPR) + AT-SW(WS-TEXSPR)) / AT-W
     COMPUTE WS-V0 = AT-Y(WS-TEXSPR) / AT-H
     COMPUTE WS-V1 = (AT-Y(WS-TEXSPR) + AT-SH(WS-TEXSPR)) / AT-H
     MOVE 0 TO WS-IN
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > WS-VN
         IF WS-VU(WS-I) >= WS-U0 - 0.00001 AND WS-VU(WS-I) <= WS-U1 + 0.00001
                 AND WS-VV(WS-I) >= WS-V0 - 0.00001 AND WS-VV(WS-I) <= WS-V1 + 0.00001
             ADD 1 TO WS-IN
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     .

*> The loaded vertices of colour WS-COLOUR: the top face of the head and of the foot (one quad each, 6 vertices) are in that colour's textures and the other colours' tops are absent.
 CHECK-TOPS.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXID
     STRING "minecraft:block/" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-COLOUR) "_bed_head_up" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXID
     PERFORM COUNT-IN
     MOVE WS-IN TO WS-HEAD-IN
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXID
     STRING "minecraft:block/" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-COLOUR) "_bed_foot_up" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXID
     PERFORM COUNT-IN
     MOVE WS-IN TO WS-FOOT-IN
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "bugbeitems " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-CLIENT-NAME) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-COLOUR) ": the head's top face (6 vertices) is in the head texture" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     MOVE 6 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-HEAD-IN TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "bugbeitems " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-CLIENT-NAME) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-COLOUR) ": the foot's top face (6 vertices) is in the foot texture" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     MOVE 6 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-FOOT-IN TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-OTHER-IN
     IF WS-COLOUR NOT = "white"
         MOVE "minecraft:block/white_bed_head_up" TO WS-TEXID
         PERFORM COUNT-IN
         ADD WS-IN TO WS-OTHER-IN
     END-IF
     IF WS-COLOUR NOT = "red"
         MOVE "minecraft:block/red_bed_head_up" TO WS-TEXID
         PERFORM COUNT-IN
         ADD WS-IN TO WS-OTHER-IN
     END-IF
     IF WS-COLOUR NOT = "blue"
         MOVE "minecraft:block/blue_bed_head_up" TO WS-TEXID
         PERFORM COUNT-IN
         ADD WS-IN TO WS-OTHER-IN
     END-IF
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "bugbeitems " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-CLIENT-NAME) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-COLOUR) ": no vertex in another colour's head texture" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-OTHER-IN TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

*> Three colours in a slot: white, red and blue draw their own top textures.
 CHECK-COLOURS.
     MOVE "slot" TO WS-CLIENT-NAME
     PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-K > 3
         EVALUATE WS-K
             WHEN 1
                 MOVE "white" TO WS-COLOUR
                 MOVE WS-WHITE TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
             WHEN 2
                 MOVE "red" TO WS-COLOUR
                 MOVE WS-RED TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
             WHEN OTHER
                 MOVE "blue" TO WS-COLOUR
                 MOVE WS-BLUE TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(1)
         END-EVALUATE
         MOVE 0 TO RL-IC-COUNT
         CALL "UI-RENDER" USING CLIENT-STATE
         PERFORM LOAD-ICONS
         PERFORM CHECK-TOPS
     END-PERFORM.

*> The hand holding a bed (the real HAND-MESH): both halves' top faces, in the colour's textures.
 CHECK-HAND.
     MOVE SCR-WORLD TO SM-SCREEN
     MOVE 0 TO CL-CAMERA CL-SWING-AT
     MOVE 1000000 TO CL-NOW-MS
     MOVE 1 TO CL-HAND-H CL-HAND-OH
     MOVE CL-NOW-MS TO CL-HAND-TICK-MS
     MOVE 1 TO PL-SLOT-COUNT(PL-HELD + 1)
     MOVE "hand" TO WS-CLIENT-NAME
     PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-K > 3
         EVALUATE WS-K
             WHEN 1
                 MOVE "white" TO WS-COLOUR
                 MOVE WS-WHITE TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(PL-HELD + 1)
             WHEN 2
                 MOVE "red" TO WS-COLOUR
                 MOVE WS-RED TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(PL-HELD + 1)
             WHEN OTHER
                 MOVE "blue" TO WS-COLOUR
                 MOVE WS-BLUE TO PL-SLOT-ITEM(PL-HELD + 1)
         END-EVALUATE
         COMPUTE CL-HAND-ITEM = PL-SLOT-ITEM(PL-HELD + 1) + 1
         MOVE 0 TO CL-HAND-KEY-COUNT CL-HAND-KEY-ITEM
         CALL "HAND-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE
         MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
         STRING "bugbeitems " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-COLOUR) " bed in the hand: whole quads, more than the 3 of a cube" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
         MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
         MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
         IF RL-HAND-COUNT > 18 AND FUNCTION MOD(RL-HAND-COUNT, 6) = 0
             MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
         END-IF
         CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
         MOVE RL-HAND-COUNT TO WS-VN
         PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > WS-VN
             MOVE RL-HAND-U(WS-I) TO WS-VU(WS-I)
             MOVE RL-HAND-V(WS-I) TO WS-VV(WS-I)
         END-PERFORM
         PERFORM CHECK-TOPS
     END-PERFORM.

*> A dropped bed (VANILLA-ITEMS-MESH, the eye above it): both halves' top faces, the quads whole.
 CHECK-GROUND.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     MOVE "item" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-ENT-TYPE WS-ROW-AREA WS-STATUS
     MOVE 64 TO WS-ENT-ID
     MOVE 10.5 TO WS-EX WS-EZ
     MOVE 64 TO WS-EY
     MOVE 0 TO WS-ENT-YAW
     CALL "GIF-SPAWN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ENT-ID WS-ENT-TYPE WS-EX WS-EY WS-EZ WS-ENT-YAW
     MOVE WS-RED TO EN-STACK-ITEM(1)
     MOVE 1 TO EN-STACK-COUNT(1)
     MOVE 0 TO CL-NOW-MS
     MOVE 10.5 TO WS-EYE(1)
     MOVE 66 TO WS-EYE(2)
     MOVE 8.5 TO WS-EYE(3)
     MOVE 0 TO RL-GI-COUNT
     CALL "VANILLA-ITEMS-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-POINT
     MOVE "bugbeitems dropped red_bed: whole quads, more than the 3 of a cube" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF RL-GI-COUNT > 18 AND FUNCTION MOD(RL-GI-COUNT, 6) = 0
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE RL-GI-COUNT TO WS-VN
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > WS-VN
         MOVE RL-GI-U(WS-I) TO WS-VU(WS-I)
         MOVE RL-GI-V(WS-I) TO WS-VV(WS-I)
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "ground" TO WS-CLIENT-NAME
     MOVE "red" TO WS-COLOUR
     PERFORM CHECK-TOPS.
 END PROGRAM TEST-SPECIAL-BED.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. GIF-SPAWN.
*> USING CLIENT-STATE, entity id, type (registry id), x y z (FLOAT-LONG), yaw (FLOAT-SHORT, also the head yaw): Add Entity.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-READY               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 1024.
 01 WS-ADD                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-UUID                PIC X(16) VALUE LOW-VALUES.
 01 WS-V0                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-V1                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-V2                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-A0                  FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-TYPE                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-X                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-Y                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-Z                    FLOAT-LONG.
 01 L-YAW                  FLOAT-SHORT.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-ID L-TYPE L-X L-Y L-Z L-YAW.
     IF WS-READY = 0
         CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
         MOVE 1 TO WS-READY
     END-IF
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-ID
     CALL "PB-PUT-UUID" USING PB-BUFFER WS-UUID
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-TYPE
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-X
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-Y
     CALL "PB-PUT-DOUBLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-Z
     CALL "PB-PUT-LPVEC3" USING PB-BUFFER WS-V0 WS-V1 WS-V2
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-A0
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-YAW
     CALL "PB-PUT-ANGLE" USING PB-BUFFER L-YAW
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-ZERO
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     CALL "ENTITY-PACKET" USING CLIENT-STATE PB-BUFFER WS-ADD
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM GIF-SPAWN.

 COPY CLTEST.
